Package: agentkeyguard
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, adduser, systemd
Recommends: openssh-client
Description: zero-credential broker for AI access to databases and servers
 AgentKeyGuard is a local credential broker. A remote agent talks to it over
 HTTP to use PostgreSQL / SSH, while the plaintext credentials only ever
 exist in the daemon memory: never returned, never written to disk, never
 placed in argv. Every operation must be approved on the owner phone.
 .
 This package installs the modular Python implementation, a systemd unit,
 and separates configuration (/etc/agentkeyguard), data
 (/var/lib/agentkeyguard) and code (/usr/lib/agentkeyguard) following the
 Filesystem Hierarchy Standard.
